    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Failing Closed: Secure Error Handling',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains failing closed, and secure error handling, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] Failing closed means that when something goes wrong, the answer is no. [[slnc 300]] Failing open means that an error becomes a yes. [[slnc 300]] It is number ten in the O W A S P top ten. [[slnc 600]] Think of a bank vault with an electronic lock. [[slnc 300]] When the power fails, the door either locks itself, or opens itself. [[slnc 300]] A vault that opens in a power cut can be opened by cutting the power. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online bank. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will hear how an error turns into an approval. [[slnc 300]] How to start every decision from no. [[slnc 300]] How to keep half done changes and leaked resources from hurting. [[slnc 300]] And how to pay for the lost availability.'),
